---
import GuidePage from '../components/GuidePage.astro';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How much does a trade name cost in Washington?', a: 'Registering a trade name costs $5 per name. You add it on your Business License Application with the Department of Revenue, either when you first apply or later.' },
  { q: 'Do I need a trade name if I have an LLC?', a: 'You need one if you do business under any name other than your exact legal LLC name, including your name without "LLC" at the end. Most Washington LLCs should register at least one for that reason.' },
  { q: 'Does a trade name protect my business name?', a: 'No. Registering a trade name lets you use it legally in Washington, but it does not give you exclusive rights to the name. If brand protection matters to you, talk to a trademark attorney.' },
  { q: 'Can I have more than one trade name?', a: 'Yes. You can register as many trade names as you need, at $5 each. That is common for businesses that run more than one brand or service line under one LLC.' },
];
---

<GuidePage
  slug="washington-trade-name-dba"
  title="Washington Trade Names (DBA): What They Are and When You Need One"
  seoTitle="Washington Trade Name (DBA): $5, and Most LLCs Need One"
  description="What a Washington trade name (DBA) is, why most LLCs need one, how it costs $5 through the Department of Revenue and how it differs from a trademark."
  eyebrow="Trade names (DBA)"
  intro="A trade name lets your business operate under a name other than its exact legal name. In Washington it costs $5, and most LLCs should have at least one."
  updated="November 2026"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <h2>What is a trade name?</h2>
  <p>
    A trade name, often called a DBA ("doing business as"), is any name your business uses that isn't its exact legal name. In Washington, trade names are registered with the <strong>Department of Revenue's Business Licensing Service</strong>, not the Secretary of State.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your LLC's legal name is the one on your Certificate of Formation, and it must include "LLC" or "Limited Liability Company." Anything else you put on a sign, a truck, a website or an invoice is a trade name.
  </p>

  <h2>Why most Washington LLCs need one</h2>
  <p>
    Say you form <strong>Cedar Ridge Landscaping LLC</strong>. If your truck, website or invoices just say <strong>"Cedar Ridge Landscaping,"</strong> that's technically a different name. That's why we always recommend registering at least one trade name: your company name without "LLC."
  </p>
  <p>You'll also want a trade name if you:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Run a second brand or service line under the same LLC</li>
    <li>Use a shorter or friendlier name than your legal name</li>
    <li>Want to open a bank account or take payments under your brand name</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How much it costs and how to register</h2>
  <p>
    Each trade name costs <strong>$5</strong>. You add it on your Washington Business License Application, either with your first application or later as an update to your existing license.
  </p>

  <h2>Trade name vs. LLC name vs. trademark</h2>
  <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto rounded-[18px] border border-[#E3ECF7] my-6">
    <table class="w-full min-w-[520px] text-left border-collapse text-base">
      <thead>
        <tr class="bg-sky2">
          <th class="p-4 font-heading text-navy"></th>
          <th class="p-4 font-heading text-navy">Registered with</th>
          <th class="p-4 font-heading text-navy">What it does</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-t border-[#E3ECF7]"><td class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy">LLC name</td><td class="p-4 text-muted">Secretary of State</td><td class="p-4">Your company's legal name. Unique among Washington business entities.</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-[#E3ECF7]"><td class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy">Trade name</td><td class="p-4 text-muted">Department of Revenue</td><td class="p-4">Lets you legally do business under another name. Does not give exclusive rights.</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-[#E3ECF7]"><td class="p-4 font-semibold text-navy">Trademark</td><td class="p-4 text-muted">State or U.S. trademark office</td><td class="p-4">Protects your brand from use by others. Talk to a trademark attorney.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>One trade name is included with our LLC formation</h2>
  <p>
    Our <strong>$400 flat-rate Washington LLC</strong> includes one trade name, usually your company name without "LLC." Additional trade names are just the $5 state fee. Already have an LLC? We can add a trade name to your existing license too. <a href="/llc">Start your LLC</a> or <a href="tel:3605292672">call 360-529-2672</a>.
  </p>
  <p class="text-base text-muted">
    This guide is general information, not legal advice. Fees are current as of November 2026 and can change.
  </p>
</GuidePage>
